                <pb facs="0318" n="312" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg312"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/5642: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in France (Tuck)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-06-09">June 9, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>364. Your 806, June 4, 5 p.m. The Department has been giving urgent consideration
                    to resumption of the North African economic program and a decision is expected
                    shortly. You may convey this information informally to the appropriate French
                    authorities.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
